# Protected paths: this file is the single source of truth for them.
# scripts/check-protected-paths.sh reads it to classify a diff as protected or unprotected,
# and `scripts/check-protected-paths.sh --validate` checks it. Use only the syntax that
# script's header documents. An agent never merges a PR that touches a protected path: one
# whose last matching line here has an owner. A line with no owner makes its path not owned
# (the later line wins, as on GitHub); only the four reference skill files may have one.

# Agent and repository configuration, docs that need the human's approval
/.github/                                   @ali-roozbahani
/.claude/                                   @ali-roozbahani
# Reference skills: not owned, so an agent may edit them; the reviewer judges the diff and
# the rule-change signal escalates a removed or rewritten rule line. Files, not directories,
# so a file added next to one of them stays protected by /.claude/.
/.claude/skills/tm-ios/SKILL.md
/.claude/skills/tm-android/SKILL.md
/.claude/skills/tm-kmp-shared/SKILL.md
/.claude/skills/tm-testing/SKILL.md
/CLAUDE.md                                  @ali-roozbahani
/docs/architecture/                         @ali-roozbahani
/docs/epics/                                @ali-roozbahani

